<title>HONG KONG: Haeco 1996 profit rises 49.3 percent.</title>
<headline>Haeco 1996 profit rises 49.3 percent.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   267.0	vs  179.0</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    54.0	 vs  54.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  155.0 gain vs  17.0 loss</p>
<p>    Net			    494.5	vs  331.3</p>
<p>    Turnover		     2,392.3    vs  2,390.8</p>
<p>    Company name		 Hong Kong Aircraft Engineering Co</p>
<p>				     Ltd (Haeco)</p>
<p>    Books close		  April 28 to May 6</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   May 12</p>
<p>NOTE - Hong Kong Aircraft is 25 percent held by Cathay Pacific Airways Ltd and 27 percent by Swire Pacific Ltd. It is engaged in the overhaul and maintenance of commercial aircraft.</p>
<p>During 1996 the company completed the formation, with a wholly-owned subsidiary of Rolls Royce Plc, of 50/50 joint venture company Hong Kong Aero Engine Services Ltd. In recognition of the volume of business and relevant interests brought to the venture by the company, Rolls Royce paid the company HK$155 million.  </p>
<p>Total dividend for year is 80 H.K. cents (including interim dividend of 26 cents) vs same.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
